              }
            ],
            "draft_status": "published",
            "enable_logs_sample": null,
            "enable_samples": null,
            "escalation_message": "",
            "evaluation_delay": 300,
            "force_delete": null,
            "group_retention_duration": "",
            "groupby_simple_monitor": null,
            "id": "314985774",
            "include_tags": true,
            "locked": false,
            "message": "{{#is_alert}}\n## P3 · Container Registry Pull Failure Anomaly\n**WHAT:** Total minus successful is the failed-pull rate — the registry publishes no failure counter directly. Failed pulls are almost always authentication (an expired pull secret or managed identity) or a throttled registry, and both stop every deployment at once.\n\n**WHERE:** {{value}} · env `stage` · region `global`\n**SERVICE:** `azure-landing-zone` (cloud / azure_container_registry, tier0)\n**BUSINESS IMPACT:** The service still functions but measurably worse; a subset of traffic or users is failing.\n**WHY IT TRIGGERED:** The signal deviated from its own learned baseline by more than the configured number of deviations — not because it crossed a fixed number.\n**OWNER:** cloud-engineering · support 24x7 · this does not page\n**RUNBOOK:** attached to this monitor as `Container Registry Pull Failure Anomaly` — open it from the monitor's Runbook asset.\n**AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS:** workflow `diag-azure-resource` has run; its output is attached to this event.\n**RELATED EVENTS:** correlated on `registry.stage.azure-landing-zone` — deployments, infrastructure changes and platform events from the last 30 minutes are attached as context.\n**SLO / ERROR BUDGET:** `slo-cloud-platform-availability` · no error-budget impact (non-production)\n{{/is_alert}}\n{{#is_warning}}\n## Container Registry Pull Failure Anomaly — warning\nApproaching the alert condition on {{value}}. Investigate before it becomes P3.\n{{/is_warning}}\n{{#is_no_data}}\n## Container Registry Pull Failure Anomaly — NO DATA\nTelemetry stopped arriving for {{value}}. Treat this as a telemetry-health incident: an unmonitored resource is worse than an alerting one.\n{{/is_no_data}}\n{{#is_recovery}}\n## Recovered · Container Registry Pull Failure Anomaly\n{{value}} returned to normal. Error-budget impact recorded against `slo-cloud-platform-availability`. No action required; the correlation group closes when every child recovers.\n{{/is_recovery}}\n{{#is_warning_recovery}}\nWarning cleared for {{value}}.\n{{/is_warning_recovery}}",
            "monitor_threshold_windows": [],
            "monitor_thresholds": [
              {
                "critical": "1",
                "critical_recovery": "",
                "ok": "",
                "unknown": "",
                "warning": "",
                "warning_recovery": ""
              }
            ],
            "name": "[P3][stage][cloud] Container Registry Pull Failure Anomaly (critical)",
            "new_group_delay": 300,
            "new_host_delay": 300,
            "no_data_timeframe": 0,
            "notification_preset_name": "",
            "notify_audit": false,
            "notify_by": [
              "subscription_name"
            ],
            "notify_no_data": false,
            "on_missing_data": "",
            "priority": "3",
            "query": "avg(last_1h):anomalies(sum:azure.containerregistry_registries.total_pull_count{env:stage,alert_band:critical,resource_type:azure_container_registry} by {subscription_name,name}.as_rate() - sum:azure.containerregistry_registries.successful_pull_count{env:stage,alert_band:critical,resource_type:azure_container_registry} by {subscription_name,name}.as_rate(), 'agile', 3, direction='above') \u003e= 1",
