            "locked": false,
            "message": "{{#is_alert}}\n## P4 · Azure Budget Utilization\n**WHAT:** Azure Budget Utilization: cost signal detected by threshold analysis.\n**WHERE:** {{value}} · env `stage` · region `global`\n**SERVICE:** `platform-services` (cloud / azure_subscription, tier0)\n**BUSINESS IMPACT:** Observability or configuration hygiene is degraded. No direct customer impact, but our ability to see or govern the estate is reduced.\n**WHY IT TRIGGERED:** 50% and 75% of a monthly budget are calendar checkpoints, not statistical ones — they only mean something against the day of the month, which the runbook covers. Informational by design: this is the layer that gives finance and engineering a shared number before anything is wrong.\n\n**OWNER:** cloud-engineering · support 24x7 · this does not page\n**RUNBOOK:** attached to this monitor as `Azure Budget Utilization` — open it from the monitor's Runbook asset.\n**AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS:** workflow `auto-finops-review` has run; its output is attached to this event.\n**RELATED EVENTS:** correlated on `finops.stage.platform-services` — deployments, infrastructure changes and platform events from the last 30 minutes are attached as context.\n**SLO / ERROR BUDGET:** `slo-platform-services` · no error-budget impact (non-production)\n{{/is_alert}}\n{{#is_warning}}\n## Azure Budget Utilization — warning\nApproaching the alert condition on {{value}}. Investigate before it becomes P4.\n{{/is_warning}}\n{{#is_no_data}}\n## Azure Budget Utilization — NO DATA\nTelemetry stopped arriving for {{value}}. Treat this as a telemetry-health incident: an unmonitored resource is worse than an alerting one.\n{{/is_no_data}}\n{{#is_recovery}}\n## Recovered · Azure Budget Utilization\n{{value}} returned to normal. Error-budget impact recorded against `slo-platform-services`. No action required; the correlation group closes when every child recovers.\n{{/is_recovery}}\n{{#is_warning_recovery}}\nWarning cleared for {{value}}.\n{{/is_warning_recovery}}",
