            "message": "{{#is_alert}}\n## P3 · Azure Budget Burn Rate Excessive\n**WHAT:** Azure Budget Burn Rate Excessive: cost signal detected by threshold analysis.\n**WHERE:** {{value}} · env `stage` · region `global`\n**SERVICE:** `platform-services` (cloud / azure_subscription, tier0)\n**BUSINESS IMPACT:** Nothing is broken yet. A boundary will be crossed if nobody acts within the lead time this monitor provides.\n**WHY IT TRIGGERED:** Burn rate is spend pace divided by the pace that would exactly consume the budget by month-end, so 1.0 is \"on plan\" by construction. 1.5 means the month ends 50% over if nothing changes — the same multi-window logic the SLO burn-rate alerts use, applied to money.\n\n**OWNER:** cloud-engineering · support 24x7 · this does not page\n**RUNBOOK:** attached to this monitor as `Azure Budget Burn Rate Excessive` — open it from the monitor's Runbook asset.\n**AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS:** workflow `auto-finops-review` has run; its output is attached to this event.\n**RELATED EVENTS:** correlated on `finops.stage.platform-services` — deployments, infrastructure changes and platform events from the last 30 minutes are attached as context.\n**SLO / ERROR BUDGET:** `slo-platform-services` · no error-budget impact (non-production)\n{{/is_alert}}\n{{#is_warning}}\n## Azure Budget Burn Rate Excessive — warning\nApproaching the alert condition on {{value}}. Investigate before it becomes P3.\n{{/is_warning}}\n{{#is_no_data}}\n## Azure Budget Burn Rate Excessive — NO DATA\nTelemetry stopped arriving for {{value}}. Treat this as a telemetry-health incident: an unmonitored resource is worse than an alerting one.\n{{/is_no_data}}\n{{#is_recovery}}\n## Recovered · Azure Budget Burn Rate Excessive\n{{value}} returned to normal. Error-budget impact recorded against `slo-platform-services`. No action required; the correlation group closes when every child recovers.\n{{/is_recovery}}\n{{#is_warning_recovery}}\nWarning cleared for {{value}}.\n{{/is_warning_recovery}}",
