            "message": "{{#is_alert}}\n## P3 · Snowflake Task Failure\n**WHAT:** Snowflake Task Failure: job_failure signal detected by threshold analysis.\n**WHERE:** {{value}} · env `stage` · region `global`\n**SERVICE:** `data-platform` (database / snowflake_account, tier0)\n**BUSINESS IMPACT:** The service still functions but measurably worse; a subset of traffic or users is failing.\n**WHY IT TRIGGERED:** A scheduled task either succeeded or it did not. Downstream tables are stale from the first failure, so there is no tolerance band to tune.\n\n**OWNER:** data-engineering · support 24x7 · this does not page\n**RUNBOOK:** attached to this monitor as `Snowflake Task Failure` — open it from the monitor's Runbook asset.\n**AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS:** workflow `remediate-rerun-job` has run; its output is attached to this event.\n**RELATED EVENTS:** correlated on `analytics.stage.data-platform` — deployments, infrastructure changes and platform events from the last 30 minutes are attached as context.\n**SLO / ERROR BUDGET:** `slo-data-freshness` · no error-budget impact (non-production)\n{{/is_alert}}\n{{#is_warning}}\n## Snowflake Task Failure — warning\nApproaching the alert condition on {{value}}. Investigate before it becomes P3.\n{{/is_warning}}\n{{#is_no_data}}\n## Snowflake Task Failure — NO DATA\nTelemetry stopped arriving for {{value}}. Treat this as a telemetry-health incident: an unmonitored resource is worse than an alerting one.\n{{/is_no_data}}\n{{#is_recovery}}\n## Recovered · Snowflake Task Failure\n{{value}} returned to normal. Error-budget impact recorded against `slo-data-freshness`. No action required; the correlation group closes when every child recovers.\n{{/is_recovery}}\n{{#is_warning_recovery}}\nWarning cleared for {{value}}.\n{{/is_warning_recovery}}",
