            "force_delete": null,
            "group_retention_duration": "",
            "groupby_simple_monitor": null,
            "id": "314985759",
            "include_tags": true,
            "locked": false,
            "message": "{{#is_alert}}\n## P3 · Host Swap Pressure\n**WHAT:** Measured as free swap FALLING against its own recent baseline, never as \"swap in use \u003e 0\". A host that has always used 10% of its swap is fine; a host that just started consuming swap is one that has run out of real memory, and its latency is about to become somebody's incident.\n\n**WHERE:** {{value}} · env `stage` · region `global`\n**SERVICE:** `compute-platform` (infrastructure / host, tier0)\n**BUSINESS IMPACT:** Nothing is broken yet. A boundary will be crossed if nobody acts within the lead time this monitor provides.\n**WHY IT TRIGGERED:** The signal changed faster than the configured percentage relative to its own recent history. Speed of degradation, not absolute level.\n**OWNER:** infrastructure-engineering · support 24x7 · this does not page\n**RUNBOOK:** attached to this monitor as `Host Swap Pressure` — open it from the monitor's Runbook asset.\n**AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS:** workflow `diag-host` has run; its output is attached to this event.\n**RELATED EVENTS:** correlated on `compute.stage.compute-platform` — deployments, infrastructure changes and platform events from the last 30 minutes are attached as context.\n**SLO / ERROR BUDGET:** `slo-infra-compute-availability` · no error-budget impact (non-production)\n{{/is_alert}}\n{{#is_warning}}\n## Host Swap Pressure — warning\nApproaching the alert condition on {{value}}. Investigate before it becomes P3.\n{{/is_warning}}\n{{#is_no_data}}\n## Host Swap Pressure — NO DATA\nTelemetry stopped arriving for {{value}}. Treat this as a telemetry-health incident: an unmonitored resource is worse than an alerting one.\n{{/is_no_data}}\n{{#is_recovery}}\n## Recovered · Host Swap Pressure\n{{value}} returned to normal. Error-budget impact recorded against `slo-infra-compute-availability`. No action required; the correlation group closes when every child recovers.\n{{/is_recovery}}\n{{#is_warning_recovery}}\nWarning cleared for {{value}}.\n{{/is_warning_recovery}}",
            "monitor_threshold_windows": [],
            "monitor_thresholds": [
              {
                "critical": "-25",
                "critical_recovery": "",
                "ok": "",
                "unknown": "",
                "warning": "-15",
                "warning_recovery": ""
              }
            ],
            "name": "[P3][stage][infrastructure] Host Swap Pressure (critical)",
            "new_group_delay": 300,
            "new_host_delay": 300,
            "no_data_timeframe": 0,
            "notification_preset_name": "",
            "notify_audit": false,
            "notify_by": [
              "cluster"
            ],
            "notify_no_data": false,
            "on_missing_data": "",
            "priority": "3",
            "query": "pct_change(avg(last_30m),last_4h):avg:system.swap.pct_free{env:stage,alert_band:critical} by {cluster,host} \u003c -25",
