            "message": "{{#is_alert}}\n## P3 · Batch Job Failed\n**WHAT:** Batch Job Failed: job_failure signal detected by threshold analysis.\n**WHERE:** {{value}} · env `stage` · region `global`\n**SERVICE:** `batch-platform` (integration / batch_job, tier0)\n**BUSINESS IMPACT:** The service still functions but measurably worse; a subset of traffic or users is failing.\n**WHY IT TRIGGERED:** A failed run is a discrete outcome.\n**OWNER:** application-development · support 24x7 · this does not page\n**RUNBOOK:** attached to this monitor as `Batch Job Failed` — open it from the monitor's Runbook asset.\n**AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS:** workflow `remediate-rerun-job` has run; its output is attached to this event.\n**RELATED EVENTS:** correlated on `batch-platform.stage.batch-platform` — deployments, infrastructure changes and platform events from the last 30 minutes are attached as context.\n**SLO / ERROR BUDGET:** `slo-batch-completion` · no error-budget impact (non-production)\n{{/is_alert}}\n{{#is_warning}}\n## Batch Job Failed — warning\nApproaching the alert condition on {{value}}. Investigate before it becomes P3.\n{{/is_warning}}\n{{#is_no_data}}\n## Batch Job Failed — NO DATA\nTelemetry stopped arriving for {{value}}. Treat this as a telemetry-health incident: an unmonitored resource is worse than an alerting one.\n{{/is_no_data}}\n{{#is_recovery}}\n## Recovered · Batch Job Failed\n{{value}} returned to normal. Error-budget impact recorded against `slo-batch-completion`. No action required; the correlation group closes when every child recovers.\n{{/is_recovery}}\n{{#is_warning_recovery}}\nWarning cleared for {{value}}.\n{{/is_warning_recovery}}",
