            "message": "{{#is_alert}}\n## P3 · Control-M Job Blocked By A Failed Predecessor\n**WHAT:** Control-M Job Blocked By A Failed Predecessor: job_failure signal detected by threshold analysis.\n**WHERE:** {{value}} · env `stage` · region `global`\n**SERVICE:** `integration-platform` (integration / controlm_job, tier0)\n**BUSINESS IMPACT:** The service still functions but measurably worse; a subset of traffic or users is failing.\n**WHY IT TRIGGERED:** A broken flow is discrete: either an upstream job in this job's condition chain ended Not OK or it did not. The judgement is made in the emitter, which is where the dependency graph actually lives.\n\n**OWNER:** application-development · support 24x7 · this does not page\n**RUNBOOK:** attached to this monitor as `Control-M Job Blocked By A Failed Predecessor` — open it from the monitor's Runbook asset.\n**AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS:** workflow `diag-dependency` has run; its output is attached to this event.\n**RELATED EVENTS:** correlated on `scheduler.stage.integration-platform` — deployments, infrastructure changes and platform events from the last 30 minutes are attached as context.\n**SLO / ERROR BUDGET:** `slo-integration-delivery` · no error-budget impact (non-production)\n{{/is_alert}}\n{{#is_warning}}\n## Control-M Job Blocked By A Failed Predecessor — warning\nApproaching the alert condition on {{value}}. Investigate before it becomes P3.\n{{/is_warning}}\n{{#is_no_data}}\n## Control-M Job Blocked By A Failed Predecessor — NO DATA\nTelemetry stopped arriving for {{value}}. Treat this as a telemetry-health incident: an unmonitored resource is worse than an alerting one.\n{{/is_no_data}}\n{{#is_recovery}}\n## Recovered · Control-M Job Blocked By A Failed Predecessor\n{{value}} returned to normal. Error-budget impact recorded against `slo-integration-delivery`. No action required; the correlation group closes when every child recovers.\n{{/is_recovery}}\n{{#is_warning_recovery}}\nWarning cleared for {{value}}