            "locked": false,
            "message": "{{#is_alert}}\n## P4 · Control-M Exporter Stopped Reporting\n**WHAT:** Control-M Exporter Stopped Reporting: telemetry_health signal detected by threshold analysis.\n**WHERE:** {{value}} · env `stage` · region `global`\n**SERVICE:** `batch-platform` (integration / controlm_server, tier0)\n**BUSINESS IMPACT:** Observability or configuration hygiene is degraded. No direct customer impact, but our ability to see or govern the estate is reduced.\n**WHY IT TRIGGERED:** Absence of any job-state observation is binary. It matters more here than in most telemetry-health archetypes: an expired Automation API session token or a stopped exporter turns every Control-M monitor green at once, which is indistinguishable from a quiet night unless something is watching the poller itself.\n\n**OWNER:** application-development · support 24x7 · this does not page\n**RUNBOOK:** attached to this monitor as `Control-M Exporter Stopped Reporting` — open it from the monitor's Runbook asset.\n**AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS:** workflow `diag-batch-job` has run; its output is attached to this event.\n**RELATED EVENTS:** correlated on `scheduler.stage.batch-platform` — deployments, infrastructure changes and platform events from the last 30 minutes are attached as context.\n**SLO / ERROR BUDGET:** `slo-batch-completion` · no error-budget impact (non-production)\n{{/is_alert}}\n{{#is_warning}}\n## Control-M Exporter Stopped Reporting — warning\nApproaching the alert condition on {{value}}. Investigate before it becomes P4.\n{{/is_warning}}\n{{#is_no_data}}\n## Control-M Exporter Stopped Reporting — NO DATA\nTelemetry stopped arriving for {{value}}. Treat this as a telemetry-health incident: an unmonitored resource is worse than an alerting one.\n{{/is_no_data}}\n{{#is_recovery}}\n## Recovered · Control-M Exporter Stopped Reporting\n{{value}} returned to normal. Error-budget impact recorded against `slo-batch-completion`. No action required; the correlation group closes when every child recovers.\n{{/is_recovery}}\n{{#is_warning_recovery}}\nWarning cleared for {{value}}.\n{{/is_warning_recovery}}",
