                "name": "Control-M Job Overrunning While Still Running",
                "resource_key": "15320574",
                "resource_type": "notebook",
                "url": "https://app.datadoghq.com/notebook/15320574"
              }
            ],
            "draft_status": "published",
            "enable_logs_sample": null,
            "enable_samples": null,
            "escalation_message": "",
            "evaluation_delay": 300,
            "force_delete": null,
            "group_retention_duration": "",
            "groupby_simple_monitor": null,
            "id": "315065776",
            "include_tags": true,
            "locked": false,
            "message": "{{#is_alert}}\n## P3 · Control-M Job Overrunning While Still Running\n**WHAT:** The only archetype in the estate that alerts on work in progress rather than on an outcome. Everything else in batch monitoring — including batch-duration-anomaly — needs the run to end before it has a value.\n\n**WHERE:** {{value}} · env `stage` · region `global`\n**SERVICE:** `batch-platform` (integration / controlm_job, tier0)\n**BUSINESS IMPACT:** The service still functions but measurably worse; a subset of traffic or users is failing.\n**WHY IT TRIGGERED:** The number is dimensionless and relative to the job's own history, which is what makes one monitor correct for four thousand jobs with wildly different runtimes. 2.0 means \"twice what THIS job's last thirty successful runs took at P95\"; 1.5 warns while there is still recovery time. An absolute number of minutes could not be shared by a 40-second file poll and a six-hour general ledger close, and one monitor per job per threshold is the monitor explosion this platform exists to prevent.\n\n**OWNER:** application-development · support 24x7 · this does not page\n**RUNBOOK:** attached to this monitor as `Control-M Job Overrunning While Still Running` — open it from the monitor's Runbook asset.\n**AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS:** workflow `diag-batch-job` has run; its output is attached to this event.\n**RELATED EVENTS:** correlated on `batch-platform.stage.batch-platform` — deployments, infrastructure changes and platform events from the last 30 minutes are attached as context.\n**SLO / ERROR BUDGET:** `slo-batch-completion` · no error-budget impact (non-production)\n{{/is_alert}}\n{{#is_warning}}\n## Control-M Job Overrunning While Still Running — warning\nApproaching the alert condition on {{value}}. Investigate before it becomes P3.\n{{/is_warning}}\n{{#is_no_data}}\n## Control-M Job Overrunning While Still Running — NO DATA\nTelemetry stopped arriving for {{value}}. Treat this as a telemetry-health incident: an unmonitored resource is worse than an alerting one.\n{{/is_no_data}}\n{{#is_recovery}}\n## Recovered · Control-M Job Overrunning While Still Running\n{{value}} returned to normal. Error-budget impact recorded against `slo-batch-completion`. No action required; the correlation group closes when every child recovers.\n{{/is_recovery}}\n{{#is_warning_recovery}}\nWarning cleared for {{value}}.\n{{/is_warning_recovery}}",
            "monitor_threshold_windows": [],
            "monitor_thresholds": [
              {
                "critical": "2",
                "critical_recovery": "",
                "ok": "",
                "unknown": "",
                "warning": "1.5",
                "warning_recovery": ""
              }
            ],
            "name": "[P3][stage][integration] Control-M Job Overrunning While Still Running (critical)",
            "new_group_delay": 300,
            "new_host_delay": 300,
            "no_data_timeframe": 0,
            "notification_preset_name": "",
            "notify_audit": false,
            "notify_by": [],
            "notify_no_data": false,
            "on_missing_data": "",
            "priority": "3",
            "query": "max(last_10m):max:controlm.job.duration_ratio{env:stage,alert_band:critical,resource_type:controlm_job,job_state:running} by {folder,job_name} * max:controlm.job.running{env:stage,alert_band:critical,resource_type:controlm_job} by {folder,job_name} \u003e 2",
            "renotify_interval": 30,
