            "include_tags": true,
            "locked": false,
            "message": "{{#is_alert}}\n## P3 · Cosmos DB Server-Side Latency Anomaly\n**WHAT:** Server-side latency excludes network and SDK time, so a deviation here is genuinely the service — which is what makes it worth separating from the application's own client-observed latency.\n\n**WHERE:** {{value}} · env `stage` · region `global`\n**SERVICE:** `database-platform` (database / azure_cosmos_db, tier2)\n**BUSINESS IMPACT:** The service still functions but measurably worse; a subset of traffic or users is failing.\n**WHY IT TRIGGERED:** The signal deviated from its own learned baseline by more than the configured number of deviations — not because it crossed a fixed number.\n**OWNER:** data-engineering · support business-hours · this does not page\n**RUNBOOK:** attached to this monitor as `Cosmos DB Server-Side Latency Anomaly` — open it from the monitor's Runbook asset.\n**AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS:** workflow `diag-database` has run; its output is attached to this event.\n**RELATED EVENTS:** correlated on `databases.stage.database-platform` — deployments, infrastructure changes and platform events from the last 30 minutes are attached as context.\n**SLO / ERROR BUDGET:** `slo-database-latency` · no error-budget impact (non-production)\n{{/is_alert}}\n{{#is_warning}}\n## Cosmos DB Server-Side Latency Anomaly — warning\nApproaching the alert condition on {{value}}. Investigate before it becomes P3.\n{{/is_warning}}\n{{#is_no_data}}\n## Cosmos DB Server-Side Latency Anomaly — NO DATA\nTelemetry stopped arriving for {{value}}. Treat this as a telemetry-health incident: an unmonitored resource is worse than an alerting one.\n{{/is_no_data}}\n{{#is_recovery}}\n## Recovered · Cosmos DB Server-Side Latency Anomaly\n{{value}} returned to normal. Error-budget impact recorded against `slo-database-latency`. No action required; the correlation group closes when every child recovers.\n{{/is_recovery}}\n{{#is_warning_recovery}}\nWarning cleared for {{value}}.\n{{/is_warning_recovery}}",
            "monitor_threshold_windows": [],
