            "message": "{{#is_alert}}\n## P3 · Security Log Source Stopped Delivering\n**WHAT:** Security Log Source Stopped Delivering: telemetry_health signal detected by threshold analysis.\n**WHERE:** {{value}} · env `stage` · region `global`\n**SERVICE:** `security-telemetry` (security / log_source, tier2)\n**BUSINESS IMPACT:** The service still functions but measurably worse; a subset of traffic or users is failing.\n**WHY IT TRIGGERED:** Absence of log delivery is binary. A silent security log source is a compliance failure and a blind spot: the control has effectively been removed even though no customer sees it.\n\n**OWNER:** security · support business-hours · this does not page\n**RUNBOOK:** attached to this monitor as `Security Log Source Stopped Delivering` — open it from the monitor's Runbook asset.\n**AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS:** workflow `diag-security-control` has run; its output is attached to this event.\n**RELATED EVENTS:** correlated on `security-telemetry.stage.security-telemetry` — deployments, infrastructure changes and platform events from the last 30 minutes are attached as context.\n**SLO / ERROR BUDGET:** `slo-security-telemetry` · no error-budget impact (non-production)\n{{/is_alert}}\n{{#is_warning}}\n## Security Log Source Stopped Delivering — warning\nApproaching the alert condition on {{value}}. Investigate before it becomes P3.\n{{/is_warning}}\n{{#is_no_data}}\n## Security Log Source Stopped Delivering — NO DATA\nTelemetry stopped arriving for {{value}}. Treat this as a telemetry-health incident: an unmonitored resource is worse than an alerting one.\n{{/is_no_data}}\n{{#is_recovery}}\n## Recovered · Security Log Source Stopped Delivering\n{{value}} returned to normal. Error-budget impact recorded against `slo-security-telemetry`. No action required; the correlation group closes when every child recovers.\n{{/is_recovery}}\n{{#is_warning_recovery}}\nWarning cleared for {{value}}.\n{{/is_warning_recovery}}",
